  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### 7.0.276\nEnh: Added mode-specific sampling managers (RawSamplingManager, RawFixedBufferSamplingManager, ValueSamplingManager, DynamicSamplingManager) for cyclic polling of PLC symbols with configurable trigger, stop, and retrieval filter predicates.\nEnh: Added generic TypedSamplingManager<T> (where T : unmanaged) for high-performance, zero-boxing sampling of unmanaged PLC values. Subscribes to ADS notifications directly and reads each payload via MemoryMarshal.Read<T>, returning TypedSampleInfo<T> samples with strongly-typed Func<TypedSampleInfo<T>, bool> trigger/stop/retrieval predicates. Use ValueSamplingManager or DynamicSamplingManager for object/dynamic structured values, and TypedSamplingManager<T> for primitive high-frequency access.\nEnh: Factored the shared session lifecycle of RawSamplingManager, RawFixedBufferSamplingManager, ValueSamplingManager, DynamicSamplingManager, and TypedSamplingManager<T> into a common ISamplingManager interface and SamplingManagerBase abstract base class (IsActive, InstancePath, DataType, IsTriggered, StoppedByCondition, Mode, StopSampling, Dispose). Added ISamplingChunkInfo / ISamplingChunkInfo<TSample> implemented by SamplingChunkInfo, RawSamplingChunkInfo, DynamicSamplingChunkInfo, and TypedSamplingChunkInfo<T>, and ISampleInfo (Timestamp) implemented by SampleInfo, RawSampleInfo, DynamicSampleInfo, and TypedSampleInfo<T>.\n### 7.0.274\nEnh: Added SamplingManager for cyclic polling of PLC symbols with configurable trigger, stop, and retrieval filter predicates. Supports typed sampling (by instance path or IValueSymbol) and raw byte sampling (by IndexGroup/IndexOffset).\nEnh: Added generic TypedSamplingManager<T> (where T : unmanaged) for high-performance, zero-boxing sampling of unmanaged PLC values. Subscribes to ADS notifications directly and reads each payload via MemoryMarshal.Read<T>, returning TypedSampleInfo<T> samples with strongly-typed Func<TypedSampleInfo<T>, bool> trigger/stop/retrieval predicates. Use SamplingManager for dynamic/string-filtered or structured values, and TypedSamplingManager<T> for primitive high-frequency access.\nEnh: Factored the shared session lifecycle of SamplingManager and TypedSamplingManager<T> into a common ISamplingManager interface and SamplingManagerBase abstract base class (IsActive, InstancePath, DataType, IsTriggered, StoppedByCondition, Mode, StopSampling, Dispose). TypedSamplingManager<T> additively gains the Mode and StoppedByCondition members. Added ISamplingChunkInfo / ISamplingChunkInfo<TSample> implemented by SamplingChunkInfo, RawSamplingChunkInfo, DynamicSamplingChunkInfo, and TypedSamplingChunkInfo<T>, and ISampleInfo (Timestamp) implemented by SampleInfo, RawSampleInfo, DynamicSampleInfo, and TypedSampleInfo<T>.\n### 7.0.272\nEnh: Added SamplingManager for cyclic polling of PLC symbols with configurable trigger, stop, and retrieval filter predicates. Supports typed sampling (by instance path or IValueSymbol) and raw byte sampling (by IndexGroup/IndexOffset).\nEnh: Added generic TypedSamplingManager<T> (where T : unmanaged) for high-performance, zero-boxing sampling of unmanaged PLC values. Subscribes to ADS notifications directly and reads each payload via MemoryMarshal.Read<T>, returning TypedSampleInfo<T> samples with strongly-typed Func<TypedSampleInfo<T>, bool> trigger/stop/retrieval predicates. Use SamplingManager for dynamic/string-filtered or structured values, and TypedSamplingManager<T> for primitive high-frequency access.\n### 7.0.109\nEnh: Overall optimizations for performance gains and less memory pressure. More internal usage of ReadOnlyMemory<byte> instead of byte[] reduces the amount of array copy operations.\n### 7.0.36\nBreaking Change: Removes .NET6 as Dependency (out-of-support)\n### 7.0\nEnh: Supports **locally** installed TwinCAT 2 (via PInvoke channel)\n     Fallback usage of 'TcAmsServer.dll' internally enables function on systems that don't have TCP Loopback port open (e.g TC2 and systems with TCP Loopback disabled), #230847\nEnh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets, TCP/IP Loopback and PInvoke\nEnh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0",
